People need to have access to information:
• For democratic engagement, such as through community councils and participatory budgeting;
• For active, free and meaningful participation in the design of policies and planning on water, sanitation and hygiene-related issues; 6 See United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2161, No. 37770, art. 6, para. 9.
• To monitor their representatives and hold them accountable;
• To make decisions about their daily use of water, sanitation and hygiene services.
